@title Ultimate Marvel vs Capcom 3 - arcade, fought deep (specials, hypers, assists, jumps)
@game  PCSE00004
@shot-every 100

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# into-a-fight.recipe's boot and menus verbatim (OFFLINE MODE -> ARCADE, Ryu, default
# assists and stage), then from f6700 FIGHTS: 240-frame cycles of a walk, an L-M-H chain,
# a Hadoken (down, down-forward, forward + square), a Shinku Hadoken hyper (the same
# motion + square+triangle), an assist call (L then R), a jump-in heavy and the S button
# (cross - which also clears every win/continue screen between fights). Each cycle is
# played once facing right and once facing left, because sides switch mid-fight.
# The point is RENDERING AND SOUND COVERAGE: hit sparks, hyper flashes and super
# backgrounds, assists entering, projectiles, round/KO screens and the next opponents.
#
# HOW IT WAS AUTHORED
# Controls from the default Vita layout (square L, triangle M, circle H, cross S, L/R
# assists; hyper = motion + two attacks). Generated - the timeline after 6700 is regular.
# The boot HOLDS at 3010 until the title screen reads the pad (`@wait call
# sceCtrlPeekBufferPositive`: f3148 native, about f4100 on a phone), and every later INPUT
# line runs late by the hold - so input frames from there on are 140 below the display frames
# they land on natively (the fight's first input, written 6560, lands near f6700). `@section`
# and `@shot` frames are display frames and do not move. Without the hold a frame-timed DOWN
# reached the PSN sign-in dialog before it existed on the phone, and every CROSS after it
# answered "sign in", which fails offline and re-asks forever.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
3000: start
3006:
3010: @wait call sceCtrlPeekBufferPositive   # the title screen starts reading the pad (f3148 native, ~f4100 phone)
3100: start
3106:
